WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.520
There's nothing quite as unsatisfying as a
bad comedy.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:08.240
An awful horror flick might provide some unexpected
laughs, and an atrocious action film might

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.620
have a few impressive stunts.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.300
But watching someone who's supposed to be
funny and failing in every possible way is

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.420
just downright painful.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.660
From pathetic sequels to ill-advised passion
projects, here are some of the cringeworthy

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.840
comedies that bombed with a zero rating on
Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.140
True Memoirs of an International Assassin

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.080
If you visit Kevin James' page on Rotten Tomatoes,
you'll see a lot of green splotches.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.950
But if you're looking for the ultimate Kevin
James calamity, then head over to Netflix

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:40.070
and check out True Memoirs of an International
Assassin, the worst-reviewed film of the comedian's

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:40.560
career.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.640
This 2016 film follows James as a schlubby
writer who pens a bestselling novel about

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.220
an international assassin.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.940
Unfortunately, his publisher is marketing
the book as nonfiction, so everybody thinks

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.840
James is a real-life assassin.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:58.460
As a result, he's kidnapped and taken to Venezuela,
where he finds himself in the middle of a

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:02.440
deadly game involving South American revolutionaries
and a Russian gangster.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.920
"I punched you.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.160
You punch like a small child.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.400
It hurt you.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:08.540
It tickled."

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:13.040
Honestly, it's not a bad premise, but the
execution is completely lackluster.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:13.740
The A.V.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.560
Club described the film as "a poor man's Edgar
Wright movie," while RogerEbert.com noted

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.900
that it keeps using the same gags over and
over.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.260
"Never bring a knife AAAAAAAHHHHHH!

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.980
You brought a knife to a gunfight!"

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.100
All Nighter

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:35.680
The 2017 film All Nighter finds J.K. Simmons
playing an ultra-manly dad whose daughter

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.860
has disappeared, so he teams up with her ex-boyfriend,
a banjo-loving hippie played by Emile Hirsch.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.340
As they look for her, they encounter a whole
host of bizarre characters while Simmons teaches

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.040
Hirsch how to be a real "man."

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.279
Aside from its very specific views on manhood,
critics agreed the movie suffers from some

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.240
shoddy directing and a weak script.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.560
"A man should know how to drive.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.160
I have a bicycle.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:01:59.740
Well, congrats on that.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:03.260
It's actually considered very masculine in
the Netherlands"

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.959
As Derek Smith of Slant Magazine put it, All
Nighter jumps back and forth from "mystery"

00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:12.890
to "mismatched-buddy movie" to "inspirational
redemptive drama," and sadly, it can't stick

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:13.900
any of its landings.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.440
Still, Simmons does his best to get audiences
laughing, because slump or no slump, the man

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.540
is always a pro.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:21.740
The Con Is On

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:27.140
The Con Is On boasts a pretty incredible cast
led by Uma Thurman, Tim Roth, Alice Eve and

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.080
Sofia Vergara.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.580
The plot revolves around Thurman as a con
artist who owes money to a dangerous kingpin,

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.560
so she decides to steal a priceless jewel
from her alcoholic husband's ex-wife.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.300
But it just can't compare to better heist
films, as it relies on "edgy" humor that really

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.700
isn't all that edgy.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.200
"You haven't ---- me."

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.860
That impressive cast actually weighs the movie
down, as the characters are just loud, eccentric,

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.780
and lacking any real human elements.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:03.660
So while it's always nice to see Uma Thurman
in action, it's hard not to wish this particular

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:07.480
film wasn't trying to con audiences into wasting
an hour and 30 minutes of their time watching

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.040
it.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.620
Surfer, Dude

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:16.100
2008's Surfer, Dude was a bit of a passion
project for Matthew McConaughey, as it combined

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:19.580
catching waves, smoking weed, and walking
around without a shirt on.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:24.300
The plot, very predictably, involves a stoned
surfer who just wants to enjoy the ocean.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:25.420
"Not feeling it.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:27.620
. Not into it.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.240
I just wanna surf.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.540
Beat the stove day to day."

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.980
Unfortunately, Mother Nature and the Man are
getting in the way, so McConaughey fights

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.480
back with the power of pot.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.960
And as this movie co-stars Woody Harrelson
and Willie Nelson, there's a whole lot of

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:42.780
ganja going on.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:46.920
Sadly, it was a complete wipeout with the
critics, but fortunately, The Lincoln Lawyer

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:51.659
came along in 2011 and saved McConaughey's
career, leaving Surfer, Dude adrift in the

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.180
sea of bad Hollywood comedies.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.760
Look Who's Talking Now

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:01.000
John Travolta's career has seen some incredible
highs and some embarrassing lows, but he arguably

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:05.109
hit rock bottom with Look Who's Talking Now,
the final installment in the Look Who's Talking

00:04:05.109 --> 00:04:05.600
trilogy.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:10.820
The series got started in 1989, with Travolta
playing a cab driver who falls in love with

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:14.920
a single mom played by Kirstie Alley, who
has a talking baby that sounds like Bruce

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:15.420
Willis.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.340
In the sequel, Alley and Travolta have a daughter
who sounds like Roseanne Barr.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:24.740
In part three, we meet two bickering dogs
voiced by Danny DeVito and Diane Keaton, who

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:25.880
eventually fall in love.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:29.480
Multiple critics slammed the movie as a ripoff
of Lady and the Tramp.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.669
But instead of of romantic spaghetti dinners,
Look Who's Talking Now is loaded with lousy

00:04:33.669 --> 00:04:37.840
quips, poop jokes, and lines that feel a little
out of place in a kid's film.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:40.400
"It's Daphneeee, you tick magnet.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:40.920
Tick magnet?

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:43.140
Like you've never sniffed a butt."

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.940
The movie also desperately tries to pad out
its running time with jaw-droppingly bad fantasy

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:51.400
sequences, one of which features a pointless
Charles Barkley cameo.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:52.940
"Can I play?

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.040
With me?

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.540
Let's get busy."

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:58.920
Homer and Eddie

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:04.800
Starring James Belushi and Whoopi Goldberg,
1989's Homer and Eddie has largely been forgotten

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.150
by comedy fans, and that's probably because
it just isn't funny.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:11.760
Sure, it tries to be, but it also wants to
be a heavy-handed drama.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.900
And while that convergence of tears and laughter
might work for some films, here it results

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:17.420
in disaster.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:22.280
The movie follows a mentally challenged man
named Homer who wants to visit his long-lost

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.920
parents, so he decides to hitchhike his way
to Oregon.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.400
Along the way, he gets picked up by Eddie,
a murderous maniac who's dying of cancer and

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.060
just escaped from a mental ward.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:35.720
Naturally, the two form a friendship, learn
about life, and give Oscar-bait performances

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:39.480
that involve a lot of screaming, squealing,
and super sappy discussions.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:44.820
"And you want me - and you want me to brush
my teeth?

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.140
You want to brush your teeth now?"

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:53.040
In between the conversations about God and
the gags involving an overweight prostitute,

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:57.479
Belushi and Goldberg's eccentricities keep
piling up until you can't help but lose your

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:57.980
mind.

